  "description_html": "Skeletal diagram of <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infernodrakon\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Infernodrakon\">Infernodrakon hastacollis</a></i> showing known fossil material of the holotype (<b>BMR P2002.2</b>) specimen. Scale bar=50 cm.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Key\">Key</h3></div>\n<p><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FFFFFF\" title=\"#FFFFFF\"> </b>=Holotype <small style=\"font-size:85%;\">(BMR P2002.2)</small><br>\n<b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#8C8C8C\" title=\"#8C8C8C\"> </b>=Unknown\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080%2F02724634.2024.2442476\">\"<i>Infernodrakon hastacollis</i> gen. et sp. nov., a new azhdarchid pterosaur from the Hell Creek Formation of Montana, and the pterosaur diversity of Maastrichtian North America\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080%2F02724634.2021.1907587\">\"Morphology and taxonomy of <i>Quetzalcoatlus</i> Lawson 1975 (Pterodactyloidea: Azhdarchoidea)\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080%2F02724634.2020.1780247\">\"Functional morphology of <i>Quetzalcoatlus</i> Lawson 1975 (Pterodactyloidea: Azhdarchoidea)\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://peerj.com/articles/2908/\">\"Neck biomechanics indicate that giant Transylvanian azhdarchid pterosaurs were short-necked arch predators\"</a></li>\n<li><i>Quetzalcoatlus lawsoni</i> skeletal by Brennon Valdez, 2022</li></ul>",
